      "content": "<h3>How LinkedHashSet works inside</h3>\n<p>LinkedHashSet is a HashSet whose internal map is a <code>LinkedHashMap</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The constructor calls <code>super(capacity, loadFactor, true)</code>, a package-private HashSet constructor that creates a <code>LinkedHashMap</code> instead of a plain HashMap.</li>\n<li>Each entry carries <code>before</code> and <code>after</code> references. The map keeps <code>head</code> (eldest) and <code>tail</code> (youngest) so iteration just follows <code>after</code> pointers.</li>\n<li>Lookups still go through the hash table, so <code>contains</code>/<code>add</code>/<code>remove</code> are O(1) like HashSet.</li>\n<li>Memory: two extra references (8 bytes with compressed pointers) per element on top of the HashMap entry.</li>\n<li>Iteration is O(size) because it ignores empty buckets (HashSet iteration is O(capacity + size)).</li>\n<li>The \"access order\" mode (for LRU caches) exists only on <code>LinkedHashMap</code>, not on LinkedHashSet.</li>\n</ul>"
