      "content": "<h3>Best practices</h3>\n<p>When and how to use LinkedHashSet well.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Choose it when you need uniqueness <strong>and</strong> a predictable order, for example to remove duplicates from a list without reordering.</li>\n<li>Prefer plain <code>HashSet</code> when order does not matter: it uses less memory.</li>\n<li>Use immutable elements and consistent <code>equals</code>/<code>hashCode</code>, as for any hash-based collection.</li>\n<li>Use <code>getFirst</code>/<code>getLast</code>/<code>reversed</code> (Java 21) instead of iterating to find the ends.</li>\n<li>For an LRU cache use <code>LinkedHashMap</code> with access order, not a set.</li>\n</ul>"
